From bbae60890ae25a2cbd39e9bbd057231e574f86f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:31:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] apps: ink/paper outlined Messaging

Squashed from:
- 0001-ink-paper-outlined-messaging
- 0002-preserve-dialog-popup-padding

Rebased onto 2026-10 lineage-23.2 heads: keep the upstream window_background
and elegantTextHeight changes beneath the E-Ink overrides.

Change-Id: Ice77ecb9d2e4affc612fcde1201624c925a60d4b

Upstream colours and bools whose only consumers the patch replaced keep their upstream values (navigation_bar_bg, light_navigation_bar, background_item_pressed, translucent_white, sim_selector_background_start/end, message_bubble_color_selected, message_error_bubble_color_incoming, chips_dropdown_background_activated/pressed, contact_picker_tab_pressed, conversation_compose_divider_start); nothing reads them.

Outgoing (and incoming) audio progress tracks are light grey under the black progress (was black on black); the former shadow gradients are single 1px lines on their casting side, and the compose divider no longer fades; dialog windows take their edge only from the window border, with 28dp corners (no second inner outline).

Bubbles, the compose field, chips, panels, attachments, widgets and buttons use whole-pixel 1dp edges (2px at 300dpi); selected bubbles, the pressed send button and activated or selected touch states are 2dp; the invalid chip is a 1dp 3dp/2dp dash. List popups and recipient suggestions are the paper-filled native nine-patch, so the popup border (FlatWindowBorder) draws their only edge. Avatars and bubbles drawn in code use round(density); dividers stay 1px.
